      {
        "id": 258056,
        "name": "Jeysie",
        "username": "Jeysie",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/{size}/1868_2.png",
        "created_at": "2024-04-23T02:00:25.976Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"TheRealPeacockTalk\" data-post=\"15\" data-topic=\"30746\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/dec6dc/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> TheRealPeacockTalk:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The only logic one can apply is that anything can happen.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I’ve been slowly plotting a letter for the eventual third shipping episode for a while now, and one of the things I was definitely going to put in it was an affectionately amused observation that the RL fandom is almost an unrealistic model for the Metaverse sometimes, because we are <em>way</em> too sane and reasonable on matters like this compared to what an actual fandom for a mass market property would be like.</p>",
